// The Scroll of imbuing, and the four Fremennik rings it can imbue.
//
// THE SCROLL IS OSRS'S OWN ITEM, obj 26706, model 45065, imported by tools/models/importosrs.py.
// In Old School it is bought from Emir's Arena for 200 points; there is no Emir's Arena in a 2006
// build, so here it DROPS - from an on-task slayer kill, and far more often from a superior. The
// two rates are in slayer.constant with the arithmetic that chose them.
//
// WHAT IT CAN IMBUE IS NOT A LIST IN A SCRIPT. Every imbueable item carries param=imbue_into
// naming its imbued twin, and every imbued item carries param=imbue_from naming the plain one it
// came from (imbue_scroll.param). So the script is one proc that reads a param, the fourteen
// recoloured helmets cost it nothing, and the pairing cannot half-exist: tools/poh_battery.py
// group 66 walks the whole obj table and fails if either direction is missing or disagrees.
//
// UNCHARGING IS OSRS'S RULE TOO - "every item can be uncharged to return the scroll in its
// original form, allowing it to be swapped to other items freely" - and it matters more here than
// it does there, because here the scroll is a rare drop rather than a shop line.
//
// THE FOUR RINGS ARE THE WHOLE OF OSRS'S SCROLL LIST THAT THIS BUILD HAS, minus the two already
// done. The scroll imbues thirteen items in Old School: the black mask and the slayer helmet (both
// imbued here since the round in claude/slayer-imbues.md), the archers, berserker, seers and
// warrior rings - all four below - and seven that do not exist in this era at all (granite ring,
// ring of suffering, ring of the gods, treasonous and tyrannical rings, and the two salve
// amulets, whose base item has no source here: the Haunted Mine is not built). The magic
// shortbow (i) and the imbued god capes are NOT on the scroll's list in Old School either, and the
// god capes already have their own source here - Mage Arena II gives them.
//
// EVERY STAT BELOW IS DOUBLE THE PLAIN RING'S OWN, which is what the wiki says the imbue does
// ("its stats are double those of the berserker ring"), and it is doubled off THIS BUILD'S rings
// rather than copied from Old School's numbers. Old School's Seers ring (i) is +12/+12 because its
// plain ring is +6/+6; ours is +4/+4, so ours is +8/+8. Copying the 12 would have left the imbued
// ring three times the ring it is an imbue of. The plain four are in scripts/_unpack/377/all.obj,
// which is also where their param=imbue_into lines live.

[slayer_imbue_scroll]
name=Scroll of imbuing
desc=A magical scroll used to imbue a variety of items.
model=obj_slayer_imbue_scroll
2dzoom=1866
2dxan=370
2dyan=1924
2dzan=1953
2dxof=-3
2dyof=3
cost=100
members=yes
stackable=yes
tradeable=no

[berzerker_ring_i]
name=Berserker ring (i)
desc=A ring reputed to bring out a berserk fury in its wearer. It has been imbued.
model=obj_berzerker_ring
iop2=Wear
iop3=Uncharge
members=yes
tradeable=no
2dxof=3
2dyof=-15
2dzoom=600
2dyan=1916
2dxan=324
wearpos=ring
weight=4g
cost=10000
param=strengthbonus,8
param=imbue_from,berzerker_ring

[warrior_ring_i]
name=Warrior ring (i)
desc=A legendary ring once worn by Fremennik warriors. It has been imbued.
model=obj_warrior_ring
iop2=Wear
iop3=Uncharge
members=yes
tradeable=no
2dxof=2
2dyof=-6
2dzoom=570
2dyan=1776
2dxan=348
wearpos=ring
weight=4g
cost=10000
param=slashattack,8
param=slashdefence,8
param=imbue_from,warrior_ring

[ranger_ring_i]
name=Archers ring (i)
desc=A fabled ring that improves the wearer's skill with a bow... It has been imbued.
model=obj_ranger_ring
iop2=Wear
iop3=Uncharge
members=yes
tradeable=no
2dxof=4
2dyof=-14
2dzoom=630
2dyan=1904
2dxan=332
wearpos=ring
weight=4g
cost=10000
param=rangeattack,8
param=rangedefence,8
param=imbue_from,ranger_ring

[seer_ring_i]
name=Seers ring (i)
desc=A mysterious ring that can fill the wearer with magical power... It has been imbued.
model=obj_seer_ring
iop2=Wear
iop3=Uncharge
members=yes
tradeable=no
2dxof=3
2dyof=-13
2dzoom=620
2dyan=1940
2dxan=340
wearpos=ring
weight=4g
cost=10000
param=magicattack,8
param=magicdefence,8
param=imbue_from,seer_ring
